<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60129" href="schedule/2015/spring/ATMS/597/60129.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="ATMS" href="schedule/2015/spring/ATMS.xml">Atmospheric Sciences</subject><course id="597" href="schedule/2015/spring/ATMS/597.xml">Special Topics in Atmos Sci</course></parents><sectionNumber>RS </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>RISK ANALYSIS Course Description:  The course is an introduction to concepts and methods of quantitative risk analysis in the Earth system.  Key concepts will include probability, impacts, risk, uncertainty, statistical estimation, and decision making.  Students will use simple risk analysis methods to apply these concepts to example problems related to drought, flooding, weather extremes, and anthropogenic climate change.  The students will learn the R programming language for statistical computing, which will be used to integrate concepts and methods using observational data sets.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>109</roomNumber><buildingName>Atmospheric Sciences Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Sriver" firstName="R">Sriver, R</instructor></instructors></meeting><meeting id="1"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>109</roomNumber><buildingName>Atmospheric Sciences Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Sriver" firstName="R">Sriver, R</instructor></in